Reason:
The incorrect use of the preprocessor directive `BSAL_NODE_ENABLE_LOAD_REPORTING` instead of `BSAL_NODE_ENABLE_INSTRUMENTATION` caused the reporting logic to be bypassed when it should have been executed. This led to improper timing and reporting in the `bsal_worker_run` function, resulting in inaccurate performance metrics. The initialization of `loop_start_in_nanoseconds` and the retrieval of `current_nanoseconds` were also affected, as they relied on the instrumentation that was not executed.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
worker->loop_end_in_nanoseconds = worker->loop_start_in_nanoseconds;
```
```c
